 # Combo variant of b9e38dc0 (index 14)
 # combo_spec: D3/3+D11/0
 # Name: 孤立像素轨迹涂边框色+颜色匹配关联
+#
+# Design analysis for the fused variant:
+# a) Concrete behavior:
+#    Each large wall component is still a funnel that floods from an inner seed and radiates
+#    through its opening. The new object is a singleton outside the opening side whose color
+#    matches that funnel's inner seed color. In the output the singleton slides straight in the
+#    funnel's radiate direction until the border; every vacated cell on that path becomes the
+#    matched funnel's wall color, while the final border cell keeps the singleton color.
+# b) Complexity calibration:
+#    A single funnel would make the color match trivial, so the generator always places two
+#    funnels with distinct wall colors and distinct seed colors. Each funnel also gets its own
+#    matched singleton, giving repeated evidence for the mapping in one grid.
+# c) Broken original assumptions:
+#    The base solver assumed one dominant wall color and that every fill-colored pixel belonged
+#    to the same interior seed. That is no longer valid. The new solver must detect every large
+#    wall component independently, find its seed inside its bbox, then treat same-colored
+#    singleton pixels outside the bbox as movers rather than seeds or obstacles.
+# d) Placement legality:
+#    The generator stamps one funnel at a time, runs the solver on the partial grid, and rejects
+#    placements whose future fill wedge overlaps an already reserved wedge. Strays are chosen
+#    from cells that lie in the matched wedge, outside the wall bbox, with a clear straight path
+#    to the border and 8-neighbor isolation in the input.
+# e) Visual observability:
+#    The solver-visible link is purely visual: the outside singleton color repeats the inside
+#    seed color, and the path color repeats the matched wall color. No ordering depends on color
+#    ids or other hidden numeric conventions.
+# f) Cleanliness:
+#    Wedges are forced to be disjoint, so wall-colored trajectories do not tangle across funnels.
+#    Obstacles are omitted in generated samples to keep the two fused dimensions legible.
+# g) Inferability:
+#    Across examples the human sees two independent pairs per grid: seed-color <-> singleton-color
+#    and wall-color <-> trajectory-color. That gives enough repeated structure to infer the fused
+#    rule from a few examples instead of treating recoloring as arbitrary.
 
