+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Fill each funnel interior, radiate through its opening, then move matched outside singletons to the edge.
 
-    return wall_infos
+    Input structure:
+    - bg is the most common color. Each funnel wall is a large single-color 8-connected component with two endpoints.
+    - Every funnel contains a small inner seed of some color inside its bbox near the closed end.
+    - Outside the opening side, isolated singletons may appear; when a singleton color matches a funnel's inner seed color,
+      it belongs to that funnel.
 
+    Rule:
+    - Solve every funnel independently: flood-fill reachable bg from its inner seed and continue the fill outward between the
+      endpoint rays, preserving any unrelated non-bg pixels.
+    - After that, move each matched singleton straight along the associated funnel's radiate direction until the grid border.
